Z||000005||Rodney||06-10-2001||10:08 PM||||When I did my automatic to a 5 speed Getrag change in my 88 Mera I left the automatic steering column in. Nice not having to push that stupid lever!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodrv6||06-10-2001||11:06 PM||||The columns for automatics have a cable that runs from the gear selector lever up to the key release portion of the column.  It keeps you from removing the key unless the shift lever is in "Park".  On manual transmission columns there is a lever behind the ignition switch that you have to push to remove the key.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
